# The root Dockerfile copies go.mod, go.sum, and the Go sources at the
# root, and nothing else. Everything below is documentation, plans,
# manifests, test data, a workstation's build output, or the media
# browser's Rust tree, which builds from its own context. Sending any
# of it to the daemon costs the build time and no build reads it; the
# two cargo target directories are the large ones, gigabytes each on a
# workstation.
.git
.github
deploy
docs
plans
testdata
local
media-browser/target
media-browser/brand/iced/target
README.md
LICENSE
/library-operator
